data: {"type": "TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT", "timestamp": 1793188245002, "messageId": "c3b102e73a", "delta": "Dioscuri has no adsorption chiller model yet. I can ask the local model to write one from a spec (a silica gel-water adsorption chiller driven by low-temperature hot water, such as the brine leaving the district-heating heat exchanger (45 to 65 °C), which makes chilled water for the cooling network (6/12 °C) and rejects its heat to cooling-tower water (25 to 30 °C)), run it in a sandbox on 14 reference cases and 9 physics checks, and show you the code and the results before anything is used. Generate it?"}

